build/install: build and install Ribbon on any base (docs/BUILDING.md, "Build and install on any base")

  build.sh      make build: this repository's native pieces and generated files, per package, into O/PACKAGE
  install.sh    make install / install-PACKAGE / uninstall: one package from its manifest
  deps.sh       the dependencies report, from the templates and deps.map
  deps.map      base-neutral names and purposes for every dependency a template declares
  manifests/    one manifest per Ribbon package: its template's do_install, line for line

Manifest lines (one directive per line; # starts a comment). A source starts with @files/ (the package's
srcpkgs/PACKAGE/files), @build/ (O/PACKAGE, what build.sh made), @dist/ (DISTDIR) or @repo/ (this repository); it
may be a glob, as the template's for loops are. A source starting with ? is optional: when it is not there the
file is left out and the install says so.

  file MODE DIR SRC [NAME]   vinstall SRC MODE DIR [NAME]
  bin SRC                    vbin SRC                (usr/bin, 755)
  license SRC [NAME]         vlicense SRC [NAME]     (usr/share/licenses/PACKAGE, 644)
  doc SRC                    vdoc SRC                (usr/share/doc/PACKAGE, 644)
  conf SRC                   vconf SRC               (etc, 644)
  man SRC                    vman SRC                (usr/share/man/manN by the suffix)
  dir DIR                    vmkdir DIR
  link PATH TARGET           ln -s TARGET PATH
  tree SRC DIR               vcopy SRC DIR           (SRC's directory copied into DIR, modes kept)
  apps SRC                   ribbon-desktop's drop-in apps loop (apps:begin .. apps:end)
  state PATH MODE OWNER GROUP  a make_dirs entry: made at install (owned so when installing as root into /)
  external PATH WHERE        a file the template installs from a third-party distfile: not installed here
  base BACKEND DIRECTIVE...  DIRECTIVE only where the base's package manager is BACKEND (pkg.sh's backend: xbps for
                             Void's xbps.d files and kernel.d hook point); RIBBON_PKG_BACKEND names it by hand
  needs VAR                  the package is built only when VAR is set (make install skips it otherwise)

After an install or uninstall onto the running system (no DESTDIR), or into DESTDIR with CACHES=1 (a root that runs
as it is), install.sh makes the base's caches again when the package put down what they index, as a package manager's
triggers do: update-desktop-database for usr/share/applications/*.desktop (GLib and xdg-mime read only its
mimeinfo.cache) and update-mime-database for usr/share/mime/packages/*.xml (tests/steps.d/90-install-caches.sh).

Every install also leaves its record on the target, /var/lib/ribbon/installed/PACKAGE.files (the paths as that
system sees them): Ribbon's tools (srcpkgs/ribbon-tools/files/lib/pkg.sh) know a package by it on a base without a
package manager they can use, and remove it by it (the live system's installer, after an install). Uninstall
removes it again.

tests/steps.d/90-install.sh holds every manifest to its template: a file a template gains or loses, a changed mode
or link, or a changed file fails the step until the manifest follows.
